  "body": "## What changed\n\nA 2D ladder whose Top is below the material standing over it - typically Top set to the first real cut under a faced top, to skip the air pass at the faced top (#514 stays as decided) - now **enters safely**: it rapids no lower than the plunge height over the remaining material and feeds the rest of the way down to its first level. Before, the entry rapided to Top + the plunge height, inside the uncut stock, and verify refused the op (`rapid move 1 travels below the clearance plane inside stock`), so the air pass could not be avoided.\n\n- `camcraft_motion::approach::Approach` gains `material_top: Option<f64>` - a runtime-only field like `center_cutting`, never saved - with `entry_top()` / `carries_stock()`.\n- The ladders read it for their first descent and their plunge-law guards: `levels` (Pocket, 2D Adaptive spiral, Offset, Circular via `Motion::with_top`; the Slot reads it too but is not carried yet), `adaptive_troch` (2D Adaptive trochoidal), and the Contour's bore side, wall-side arc entry, graze, tab and ring dives.\n- `camcraft_app::operation::top_stock::carried` reads the material top over the op's region - the declared stock's highest surface there, lowered by what the program ahead cut (the reading #104's \"Top below stock\" note already made); a Contour beside a wall (Outside/Auto) reads the band one tool diameter around its region (`contour_reach`), never the part's own footprint.\n- **Only where needed:** `generate` first makes the op as before; only if that path's entry rapids down under the material standing under the tool's disc (`top_stock::dives_into`: the declared stock's own top there, lowered by the program ahead - the rapid law's #1091 and #96 re-reads) is it generated again with the top carried. Pocket, 2D Adaptive, Offset, Circular and Contour (selection and model sources; upright frames only). A finish entering through what a rough cleared keeps its path byte for byte.\n- The op says so: `Carried stock: the operation's top Z.. is below the material over its region (Z..) - the first descent starts over that material and feeds down; the first level engages .. mm`, in place of the #104 warning for those kinds. Slot, trochoidal slot, chamfer, trace and 3D kinds keep the #104 note and the rapid law's refusal.\n- Top on the material: nothing carried, the path is byte-identical (pinned).\n\n## Severity (re-judged from the code)\n\nNot P1: the rapid law convicts this entry (`RapidInStock` holds the post) and the #96/#1091 re-reads only acquit what the program ahead really cleared - a legal program refused with a workaround, P3 by the table (labels left to the maintainer). A silent case next to it - a clearance plane set inside the stock is never judged by the rapid law and posts - is filed as **#2121 (P1)**.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New `crates/app/tests/carried_stock_entry.rs` (the issue's repro: 100 x 60 x 10 plate, Ø40 bore, stock 0.5 taller, faced to the part top, Top 4 mm under it, stepdown 4):\n  - `adaptive_spiral_with_top_under_the_faced_top_feeds_through_the_carried_stock`\n  - `adaptive_trochoidal_with_top_under_the_faced_top_feeds_through_the_carried_stock` (microlift and retract returns)\n  - `contour_inside_with_top_under_the_faced_top_feeds_through_the_carried_stock` (Plunge, Helix, Ramp)\n  - `top_at_the_faced_top_carries_nothing_and_keeps_its_path`\n  - `a_finish_after_the_rough_enters_through_the_cleared_bore_unchanged`\n  Each asserts: no rapid under the plunge height over the faced top before the first level, the first move under the faced top is a feed, no level above Top, verify clean, the program posts. The three carried tests fail on main (`rapid 1 ends at z 8.000, under 12.000`).\n- Law suites whose fixture was exactly this entry (a contour or pocket with Top under a taller block): `ladder_entry_height.rs` now pins Pocket/Contour entering over the block and posting (`a_pocket_or_contour_under_a_taller_block_enters_over_it_and_posts`) and keeps the Bore's refusal; `vertical_rapid_stock.rs` and `carried_verify.rs` drive the rapid law with a Slot beside the part (not carried) - the flipped-setup case, which machines no slot, pins the contour entering over the flipped body instead (`a_flipped_carry_judges_the_entry_against_the_flipped_body`).\n- `crates/app/tests/top_stock.rs` updated: the contour now carries the stock (`generation_carries_the_stock_over_top_and_names_it`, the partial-face and narrow-mesh cases read the new note); the #104 note and rapid gate are pinned on a Slot, which does not carry (`a_slot_does_not_carry_the_stock_and_keeps_the_note_and_the_rapid_gate`).\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green on the final head (motion 389 s, app 854 s, ui 17 s); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean\n\n## The user's end-cap project (a copy, never the original)\n\n`camcraft-cli script` loading `endcap.camproj`, regenerating all 8 ops by name, posting and verifying: all ops ok, gate ok, and the program is **byte-identical** to the same run on main + #1557 (no op there has its Top below the material over it - the bore adaptive keeps its air level at the faced top, as the issue says; the entry moves did not change). An earlier build of this branch that carried on the region-wide reading alone did change 6 entry rapids (bore and profile finishes, to 1.5 mm over the faced top) - that is what the dive test replaced.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Slot / trochoidal slot / chamfer / trace / 3D kinds (not carried, see the decision file).\n- A tilted (3+2) frame: carried is off there.\n\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/1559-entry-over-carried-stock.md`.\n\nChangelog: 2D Pocket, Adaptive, Offset, Circular and Contour with Top below the material over them now start the entry over that material and feed down through it, instead of rapiding into the stock (the op was refused); a `Carried stock:` note says so\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1559\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
